## Findings fixed

### R5-F1 (MAJOR): "not called in Phase 1" for the two `--agent-wait` templates had no test

Three edits, each anchored by quoted text. No new test file, no new test name, no deviation row, no open item.

| Edit | Anchor (old text) | Change | Line after change |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1. Section 7.3, decision paragraph on `worktree list` and `worktree current` (M3) | "The NFR-003 recording test asserts zero argv for both." | Now "The NFR-003 full-sweep recording test asserts zero argv for both, and also for both `worktree ps --agent-wait` templates, so all four templates marked "not called in Phase 1" are never issued by a sweep." Added: "That wording is a design statement; R5 only allowed the two `--agent-wait` templates." | `docs/designs/orchestrator-mode.md:555` |
| 2. Section 11, `tests/sweep/test_probes_allowlist.py` row, "Full-sweep recording" sentence | "zero argv for `worktree list` and `worktree current`;" | Now "zero argv for all four templates marked "not called in Phase 1" (`worktree list`, `worktree current` and both `worktree ps --agent-wait` forms, with and without `--json`);" | `docs/designs/orchestrator-mode.md:759` |
| 3. Section 13, `### Fix cycle 3` table, R5 row | "...the allowlist pin and the version-scoped claim (Orca 1.4.245) are kept (2.2, 4, 7.3, 11, 12, 13, 15.1) |" | Replaced the closing "are kept" clause with "are kept. Gate fixes: the full-sweep recording test now asserts zero argv for both `worktree ps --agent-wait` templates as well as for `worktree list` and `worktree current`, so the "not called in Phase 1" statement is tested for all four templates (7.3, 11)" followed by the original section list. | `docs/designs/orchestrator-mode.md:1047` |

